from gk_c import G,g
H="History"; MH="Modern History"; AH="Ancient History"; WH="World History"; AC="Art & Culture"; PO="Polity"; CA="Current Affairs"
S1="Single MCQ"; S2="2-Statement Combination"; S3="3-Statement Combination"; S4="4-Statement Combination"
g(121,"The annual session of the Indian National Congress in December 1929 was held in :",["Surat","Lahore","Amritsar","Tripura"],"B",H,MH,"Indian National Movement","Lahore session 1929",S1,"E","The December 1929 Lahore session under Jawaharlal Nehru adopted the Purna Swaraj resolution.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(122,"Shortughai, a Harappan trading post in Afghanistan, was important to the Harappans for the possible supply of :",["Conch shells","Iron","Copper","Lapis lazuli and camel"],"D",H,AH,"Indus Valley Civilization","Harappan trade sites",S1,"M","Shortughai near the Oxus lay close to the lapis lazuli mines of Badakhshan; lapis was the main item.\nAnswer: (d)")
g(123,"Which of the following statements are correct regarding the demands of the protest movement known as Luddism (1811 – 17) ?\nI. A minimum wage for workers.\nII. The right to form trade unions so that they could legally present their demands.\nIII. The use of machinery for efficient labour-saving production.\nSelect the answer using the code given below :",["I and II only","II and III only","I and III only","I, II and III"],"A",H,WH,"Industrial Revolution","Luddite movement",S3,"M","The Luddites demanded a minimum wage and the right to form unions; they opposed, not demanded, labour-saving machinery.\nAnswer: (a)")
g(124,"Consider the following statements regarding the Industrial Revolution in Britain :\nI. At the beginning of industrialization, coal and iron ore were plentifully available in Britain.\nII. The blast furnace came into use at the beginning of the 18th century.\nIII. Britain was lucky in possessing excellent coking coal and high-grade iron ore in the same basins.\nWhich of the statements given above are correct ?",["I and II only","II and III only","I and III only","I, II and III"],"D",H,WH,"Industrial Revolution","Resources and technology of British industrialisation",S3,"M","All three are standard points: abundant coal and iron, Darby's coke blast furnace c.1709, and co-located coking coal and iron ore.\nAnswer: (d)")
g(125,"Which one of the following inscriptions records the history of a guild of silk weavers ?",["The Hathigumpha inscription","The Mandasor inscription","The Kudumiyamalai inscription","The Udayagiri Cave inscription"],"B",H,AH,"Literature, Science & Inscriptions","Guild inscriptions",S1,"E","The Mandasor inscription (c. 5th century CE) records the migration and history of a silk weavers' guild.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(126,"Match List I with List II :\nList I (Event): I. Passing of the Age of Consent Bill; II. Establishment of the Arya Samaj; III. Death of Dayanand Saraswati; IV. Foundation of the Nagari Pracharini Sabha\nList II (Year): A. 1893; B. 1883; C. 1875; D. 1891\nSelect the answer using the code given below :",["I-D, II-C, III-B, IV-A","I-C, II-D, III-A, IV-B","I-D, II-C, III-A, IV-B","I-C, II-D, III-B, IV-A"],"A",H,MH,"Socio-Religious Reform","Dates of reform events","Match the Following","M","Age of Consent Act 1891; Arya Samaj 1875; Dayanand died 1883; Nagari Pracharini Sabha 1893.\nAnswer: (a)")
g(127,"Consider the following statements with regard to the types of land listed in the Amarakosha.\nI. Devamatrika refers to land watered by rain.\nII. Aprahata refers to fallow land.\nIII. Pankila refers to highly fertile land.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct ?",["I and II only","II only","I and III only","I, II and III"],"A",H,AH,"Society, Economy & Trade","Land classification in the Amarakosha",S3,"H","Devamatrika is rain-fed and aprahata is fallow. Pankila is muddy or marshy land, while urvara is the fertile category, so III is wrong. Medium confidence on the glossary.\nAnswer: (a)")
g(128,"Consider the following statements regarding the role of political parties in modern democracies :\nI. In most democracies, elections are fought mainly among the candidates put up by political parties.\nII. Political parties put forward different policies and programmes and the voters choose from them.\nIII. Political parties shape public opinion.\nWhich of the statements given above are correct ?",["I and II only","II and III only","I and III only","I, II and III"],"D",PO,"Elections","Political Parties & Anti-Defection","Role of political parties",S3,"E","All three are standard NCERT statements on political parties.\nAnswer: (d)")
g(129,"Consider the following statements with regard to the Lahore Session :\nI. The Congress decided to observe Independence Day on 26 January 1930.\nII. It was decided to hoist the National Flag and sing patriotic songs at different venues.\nIII. Gandhiji suggested that the event be held synchronously in all the places.\nWhich of the statements given above are correct ?",["I and II only","II and III only","I and III only","I, II and III"],"D",H,MH,"Indian National Movement","Lahore Session and Independence Day pledge",S3,"M","The NCERT account of the Lahore Session and the 26 January 1930 observance contains all three points.\nAnswer: (d)")
g(130,"Consider the following statements :\nI. The Kailasanatha temple of Kanchi is the earliest Pallava temple hewn from solid rock.\nII. The Vaikuntha Perumal temple at Kanchi is a rare Pallava temple dedicated to Lord Vishnu.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct ?",["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"B",H,AC,"Architecture & Archaeology","Pallava temples",S2,"M","The Kailasanatha temple is a structural temple of Rajasimha, not the earliest rock-cut Pallava temple. The Vaikuntha Perumal temple is a Vishnu temple.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(131,"Consider the following pairs with reference to the Constitution of India :\nI. Part V : The Union\nII. Part X : The Scheduled and Tribal Areas\nIII. Part XII : Relations between the Union and the States\nIV. Part XIV : Amendment of the Constitution\nHow many of the pairs given above are correctly matched ?",["One","Two","Three","All four"],"B",PO,"Constitutional Framework","Constitutional Structure","Parts of the Constitution","Statement Count","M","Part V (Union) and Part X (Scheduled and Tribal Areas) are correct.\nPart XI deals with Centre-State relations, Part XII with finance and Part XIV with services, and amendment is Part XX.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(132,"With reference to the Panchsheel, which of the following is/are correct ?\nI. Mutual respect for territorial integrity and sovereignty\nII. Mutual non-interference\nIII. Collective security against non-aggression\nIV. Peaceful co-existence\nSelect the answer using the code given below :",["I only","I, II and III","II, III and IV","I, II and IV"],"D","International Relations","International Politics","Core Concepts of International Politics","Five Principles of Panchsheel",S4,"E","Panchsheel: mutual respect for sovereignty, non-aggression, non-interference, equality and mutual benefit, peaceful co-existence. Collective security is not among them.\nAnswer: (d)")
g(133,"Consider the following statements related to national integration :\nI. The expression of regional issues is not a part of democratic politics.\nII. Nation-building is an ongoing process.\nIII. Regional imbalance is associated with India's development experience.\nIV. Regions together form the nation.\nWhich of the statements given above are correct ?",["II, III and IV","I, II and IV","III and IV only","II and III only"],"A",PO,"Political Theory","Political Concepts & Ideologies","National integration and regionalism",S4,"M","Regional issues are a normal part of democratic politics, so I is wrong; II, III and IV follow NCERT.\nAnswer: (a)")
g(134,"Consider the following statements regarding UN reforms :\nI. India demands an expanded Security Council.\nII. India does not support an increase in non-permanent members.\nIII. The majority of the UN General Assembly members are from developing countries.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct ?",["I only","II only","I and II","I and III"],"D","International Relations","International Organisations","UN System & Multilateral Institutions","UN Security Council reform",S3,"M","India seeks expansion in both permanent and non-permanent categories, so II is wrong; I and III are correct.\nAnswer: (d)")
g(135,"Which one of the following Five-Year Plan documents was titled as 'Towards Faster and More Inclusive Growth' ?",["Eighth Plan","Ninth Plan","Tenth Plan","Eleventh Plan"],"D","Economy","Development & Welfare","Economic Planning","Five-Year Plan themes",S1,"E","The approach paper to the Eleventh Plan (2007-12) was titled Towards Faster and More Inclusive Growth.\nAnswer: (d)")
g(136,"Consider the following statements regarding the PESA Act, 1996 :\nI. Gram Sabhas have the power to declare Scheduled Areas.\nII. Gram Sabhas have the powers related to the management of community resources.\nIII. The PESA applies to all States except areas under the Fifth Schedule.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are not correct ?",["I and II","II and III","I and III","II only"],"C",PO,"Local Government","Panchayati Raj","PESA Act 1996",S3,"M","Scheduled Areas are declared by the President, so I is wrong. PESA applies to Fifth Schedule areas, so III is wrong. II is correct.\nStatements I and III are not correct.\nAnswer: (c)")
g(137,"Which one of the following is neither a constitutional nor a statutory body ?",["Finance Commission","NITI Aayog","National Green Tribunal","Union Public Service Commission"],"B",PO,"Constitutional & Statutory Bodies","Extra-Constitutional Bodies","Types of institutions",S1,"E","Finance Commission and UPSC are constitutional, the NGT is statutory, and NITI Aayog was set up by an executive resolution.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(138,"Which one of the following committees recommended constitutional recognition for local bodies ?",["K. Hanumanthaiah Committee","Veerappa Moily Committee","P.K. Thungon Committee","Kasturirangan Committee"],"C",PO,"Local Government","Panchayati Raj","Committees on Panchayati Raj",S1,"M","The L.M. Singhvi and P.K. Thungon committees recommended constitutional recognition of local bodies; Thungon is the one listed.\nAnswer: (c)")
g(139,"The anti-defection provisions were incorporated in the Constitution through which one of the following Constitutional Amendments ?",["50th Amendment","52nd Amendment","58th Amendment","61st Amendment"],"B",PO,"Elections","Political Parties & Anti-Defection","Tenth Schedule",S1,"E","The 52nd Amendment (1985) added the Tenth Schedule.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(140,"Consider the following statements regarding the Neighbourhood First Policy :\nI. India provides high-impact community development projects to Afghanistan.\nII. Bhutan is India's key maritime neighbour and vital partner in Vision MAHASAGAR.\nIII. India launched Operation Brahma to provide relief following an earthquake in Myanmar.\nWhich of the statements given above are correct ?",["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"B",CA,"International Relations","Bilateral Relations","Neighbourhood First Policy",S3,"M","Bhutan is landlocked, so II is wrong. India runs high-impact community development projects in Afghanistan, and Operation Brahma was the March 2025 relief to Myanmar.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(141,"India has engaged in an agreement to supply BrahMos missiles to which of the following countries ?\nI. Indonesia\nII. Philippines\nIII. Singapore\nIV. Vietnam\nSelect the correct answer using the code given below :",["I, II and III","I, III and IV","I, II and IV","II and IV only"],"C",CA,"Defence & Security","Defence Procurement & Industry","BrahMos exports",S4,"M","Philippines (2022 contract), Indonesia (2026 deal) and Vietnam (signed, confirmed May 2026). Singapore has no BrahMos agreement.\nAnswer: (c)")
g(142,"Ramanujan Fellowship is an initiative of the Department of Science & Technology, Government of India. It was launched under the :",["Research, Development and Innovation Fund","Anusandhan National Research Foundation","National Quantum Mission","National Supercomputing Mission"],"B",CA,"Science & Technology","Science Institutions & Programmes","Research fellowships",S1,"M","The fellowship, earlier run by SERB, is now administered by the Anusandhan National Research Foundation. Medium confidence because the stem says launched under.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(143,"Which of the following countries is not a member of the International Big Cat Alliance ?",["France","Somalia","Sri Lanka","Saudi Arabia"],"A",CA,"Environment & Ecology","Biodiversity & Wildlife","International Big Cat Alliance",S1,"M","Somalia and Sri Lanka are members, and Saudi Arabia joined on 22 May 2026 as the 26th member. France is not in the published member list.\nAnswer: (a)")
g(144,"Consider the following statements regarding the 'Green Nobel' :\nI. It is given every alternate year.\nII. In 2026, six winners were chosen and one of the winners is from Asia.\nIII. All the winners of 2026 are women.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct ?",["I only","II only","III only","II and III"],"D",CA,"Awards, Appointments & Personalities","International Awards","Goldman Environmental Prize",S3,"M","The Goldman Prize is annual. 2026 had six winners, all women, including Borim Kim of South Korea (Asia).\nAnswer: (d)")
g(145,"Which two countries signed a $ 2.6 billion uranium supply agreement in March 2026 ?",["India and Russia","India and Canada","India and Australia","Australia and Canada"],"B",CA,"Economy & Finance","Energy & Strategic Resources","Uranium supply deals",S1,"M","Cameco signed a C$2.6 billion supply contract with India's Department of Atomic Energy during Mark Carney's visit.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(146,"Consider the following statements regarding Exercise DUSTLIK-2026 :\nI. It is a joint military exercise between India and UAE.\nII. Its aim is to foster military cooperation and enhance combined capabilities to execute joint operations in semi-mountainous terrain.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct ?",["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"B",CA,"Defence & Security","Military Exercises","Bilateral military exercises",S2,"M","Dustlik is the India-Uzbekistan exercise, so I is wrong. II describes its aim. Not re-verified on the web; rests on prior knowledge of the exercise.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(147,"Which of the following statements about 'Vayu Shakti-2026' is/are correct ?\nI. The Vayu Shakti-2026 exercise took place in Jaisalmer, Rajasthan.\nII. Advanced fighter aircraft of the Indian Air Force, including Rafale, HAL Tejas and Mirage 2000 carried out strikes.\nIII. Boeing Apache and Boeing Chinook helicopters participated in this exercise.\nSelect the answer using the code given below :",["I, II and III","I and III only","II and III only","I only"],"A",CA,"Defence & Security","Military Exercises","IAF Vayu Shakti 2026",S3,"E","The President's press release confirms Pokhran, Jaisalmer; strikes by Rafale, Tejas and Mirage 2000; and Apache and Chinook participation.\nAnswer: (a)")
g(148,"Which of the following statements related to water governance is/are correct ?\nI. River Basin Management (RBM) is a Central Sector Scheme under the Ministry of Jal Shakti, Government of India.\nII. The major objectives of the RBM Scheme focus on promoting the use of water for domestic use.\nIII. The Brahmaputra Board is one of the key implementing agencies of the RBM.\nSelect the answer using the code given below :",["I, II and III","I and III only","II and III only","II only"],"B",CA,"Polity & Governance","Government Schemes & Policies","River Basin Management Scheme",S3,"M","I and III are confirmed by PIB. The scheme objectives are sustainable use supporting irrigation, hydropower and flood management, not domestic use, so II is wrong. Medium confidence on II.\nAnswer: (b)")
g(149,"Which of the following statements regarding the Khelo India Tribal Games is/are correct ?\nI. The inaugural edition of the Khelo India Tribal Games was organized in two States : Jharkhand and Odisha.\nII. 'Morveer' was the official mascot of these games.\nIII. The Khelo India Tribal Games are part of the Khelo India Scheme.\nSelect the answer using the code given below :",["I, II and III","I and II only","II and III only","III only"],"C",CA,"Sports","Major Sporting Events","Khelo India Tribal Games",S3,"M","The inaugural games were held in Chhattisgarh, so I is wrong. Morveer was the mascot and the games sit under the Khelo India Scheme.\nAnswer: (c)")
g(150,"Consider the following statements :\nI. Over 60% of defence equipment sourced by the Armed Forces of India is now produced domestically.\nII. The Indian defence focus is on scale, resilience and indigenous capability.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct ?",["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"C",CA,"Defence & Security","Defence Procurement & Industry","Indigenisation of defence production",S2,"M","Government figures put domestic production at about 65 percent, so over 60 percent holds, and II is the stated policy focus.\nAnswer: (c)")
# normalise: rows missing difficulty
out=[]
for r in G:
    if len(r)==10:
        r=r[:9]+("E" if r[8]=="Single MCQ" else "M",)+r[9:]
    out.append(r)
G[:]=out
if __name__=="__main__":
    from collections import Counter
    print(len(G),Counter(len(r) for r in G),sorted(set(r[0] for r in G))==list(range(51,151)))
    print(Counter(r[3] for r in G))
